      "role": "user",
      "content": "the idea of \"storytelling that feels like it's been unfolding for centuries\" is powerful. it gives the whole movement a sense of weight that the labels can't fight. they can fight a person, but they can't fight a lineage.\n\ncan you help me refine that narrative? i want to bridge the gap between my \"lost\" years in the 2011 scene and this \"ancient\" feeling. how can i frame my original work not just as tracks i wrote, but as the \"primordial sound\" that the industry has been trying to domesticate and dilute ever since? i need the language to feel like i'm uncovering a lost truth rather than just making a comeback.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
